 "verdict": "dead",
 "notes": "Gao-Han-Li-Zhou sign-of-r1 last-half-hour momentum (prev-close ref, no threshold, 15:30 -> 15:58, 0.4 ATR stop) restricted to macro days (08:30 two-bar range >= 3x rolling-60 median, or FOMC statement day from a table verified on federalreserve.gov 2013-2026). Flags helper strategies/_cal_flags.py written here. Fixed defaults: MNQ MAIN 64 trades / +566 / PF 1.16 / Sharpe 0.30; PRIOR 81 / +573 / PF 1.19; 2015-24 403 / +549 / PF 1.05. MES MAIN PF 1.03, PRIOR 1.33, 2015-24 0.94. Contrast (the finding): macro_only beats non_macro in every period on both contracts (MNQ 2015-24 +1.4 vs -4.9 per trade; 2025-26 +8.8 vs -3.0), but days=all is dead net of costs everywhere (PF 0.68-0.97) and macro_only alone is PF ~1.05 over ten years. Controls: always_long(days=all) on MNQ 2025-26 = +2,998 / PF 1.18 (long-biased tape; the macro_only +566 is smaller than that), negative on 2023-24 and 2015-24. 2025-26 macro_only P&L is the FOMC table: 14 FOMC trades +1,696 vs 50 08:30-macro trades -1,130 (MNQ); fomc_only is PF 0.79 on 75 trades 2015-24 -> a 14-trade streak. Grid: MNQ MAIN/PRIOR PF rank corr 0.61 with 7/16 cells positive on both (all macro_only); MES -0.11, 2/16. Walk-forward OOS 2025-01..2026-09 (MNQ): 234 trades, net -498, PF 0.946, Sharpe -0.22, 11/21 positive months, maxDD -1,686; whole OOS 2023-26 PF 0.935. Lucid on the OOS stream: 5 micros pass 0.033, P(first payout) 0, exp net -146 = lower bound = zero-edge control -> not recommended. Caveat: the WF 30-trade IS minimum removed the macro_only cells in many folds (35-45 trades/yr) and forced days=all in 6/15 folds; the macro_only folds net +744 on 50 trades, still noise. Verdict dead (WF PF < 1.03). Reusable output: the flags module and the contrast result (macro-day gate moves last-half-hour momentum from negative to break-even per micro).",
